 {:seon.task/name "seon-agents-answers-what-is-live"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the printer audit (docs/render.md; owner, 2026-10-25: not generating crap). ```seon.server/agents-answer``` answers every one of main's 676 tasks (30,897 tokens printed whole once its empty keys are left out; 41,434 before), almost all :held with no runs, so the reply budget shows 95 held tasks alphabetically and an outside agent never sees what is running (docs/parity.md: too much context). Correct: the live agents, the tasks running or with runs, newest first, then the rest counted by execution with the form that lists them ((seon.server/task-summaries db) filtered), as root's context groups what repeats. Proof: on a root with one running task among many held ones, the seon_agents text names the running task before any held one and counts the held."
  :seon.task/kind :work
